# Analytics core V1 scope

This repo holds a **source-agnostic analytics engine** (`analytics`, repo root) plus two adapters:

- `web/` (`analytics-web`): minimal local PoC review UI, login-free, throwaway. Do not extend it into the product.
- `app/` (`octa-app`, working title Octa): the B2B product app, built package by package along `docs/roadmap.md`. Accounts, organisations, sessions, locale, jobs and the control-plane DB belong **there**, never in `analytics`.

Do not add to `analytics` or to `web/`: auth, billing, multi-tenancy, cloud/k8s, scheduling, or SaaS infrastructure. Extra DB connectors (Oracle, SQL Server, SAP, …) stay out everywhere.

## Architecture

- Analytics logic (profiling, relationships, identities, semantic model, KPIs, query planner, reports) must not import PostgreSQL, HTTP frameworks, or HTML. `app/tests/boundary.rs` guards this.
- `web/` and `app/` may use Axum and must call only the public `analytics` API.
- All source access goes through `DataSource`. Current adapters: `FixtureConnector`, `PostgreSQLConnector`.
- The fixture path is the primary development and test path.
- Every relationship, KPI, identity, and report suggestion needs a confidence score plus human-readable evidence/reason. No black-box decisions.
- The core must work without an LLM.
- Identity templates, dictionary packs, and similar catalogs must grow when tests reveal a missing pattern. Policy: `docs/model-review.md`.

## Fixtures

`ground_truth.json` is only for the benchmark harness. Connectors and the analysis pipeline must not read it.
